In article <1989Sep11.074321.3310@iesd.auc.dk> chris@iesd.auc.dk (Christian J. Callsen) writes:
>I've encountered some problems :
>
>1) My .exe-file is 580 K WITH NO OPTIONS SET !!!!!
>   It seems to load well, though (i stripped my AT to 597xxx bytes free!!).
>   How much additional memory is needed to house nethack's variables apart
>   from the size of the .exe file ??

Although the filesize is large, the load size is smaller.  Use some utility
like MINLOAD.EXE from SIMTEL20 to determine how much RAM you actually need to
run the game.  Also, don't use the /EXEPACK option with LINK.  It actually
increases the RAM used to load the game.  The file will be bigger, but will
requite about 20K less RAM to load.

>2) When playing, H's from the "cm"-termcap-entry keep appearing on the
>   screen. Looks awful. Why ?

This is due to a missing null character in one of the termcap routines.  Mike
Threepoint posted a fixed version of thtermlib files.  You could also compile
the game with ANSI_DEFAULT defined.

>3) WHY DOESN'T THE KEYS HAVE THEIR USUAL PLACE (grrr....)
>   Is there somewhere where the cursor-arrows can be switched off, or
>   is it some kinda option ???

It is an option in the TERMCAP.CNF file.  Change the number_pad option to
!number_pad, or use the 'O' command and change it while the game is running.


